  <goal>
    Delete the H3EntraAppRegHandler shared-app-registration branch — the Model 1 code path that references
    a pre-existing shared multitenant BFF app-reg and creates zero new objects — so that H3 provisions
    ONE Entra app registration per customer, UNCONDITIONALLY, in both models. This closes the code-vs-D-13
    contradiction called out on the first page of [INCOMING-D12-D13-REMEDIATION.md](../INCOMING-D12-D13-REMEDIATION.md):
    "H3EntraAppRegHandler currently does the OPPOSITE for Model 1". Per D-13 (BINDING per owner, re-affirmed
    2026-09-28): every customer gets their own Entra app registration for the BFF API, in both models —
    Model 1 (Spaarke's tenant) + Model 2 (customer's tenant). One app-reg, one customer. No sharing.

    Per INCOMING §5 Item 1 — the docs already say this: `SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md` H3 row already
    documents the output as `appreg-{customerId}-{tenantId}`; the guide and the code have disagreed since
    before D-13 existed. This task closes that gap.

    OUT OF SCOPE (Item 2 will handle): the `Model1Shared` string literal itself — it remains a VALID
    tenancy value post-Item-1 (RunsEndpointsTests, H1SubscriptionReadinessHandler, H2a/H2b/H12c stack
    selection, ArmCostEnvelopeChecker still use it). Item 2 introduces the shared `TenancyModel` enum
    with parse-or-reject and removes the string literal comparisons everywhere in one atomic change.
    Item 1 ONLY removes H3's shared-app-reg BRANCH — it does NOT remove the tenancy literal.
  </goal>

