  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-13 (BINDING, owner-decided 3×)">
      Every customer gets their own Entra app registration for the BFF API, in both models. `SharedBffAppRegistrationId`
      is a RETIRED artifact. This decision is CLOSED — do NOT re-litigate. See
      `projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/D-13-per-customer-bff-app-registration.md`. Per its §1: "One app
      registration, one customer. No sharing."
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="D-13 §2 Dataverse ownership chain">
      The BFF writes to Dataverse app-only (S2S), as an application user. The business unit a BFF-created record
      lands in is fully determined by which application user wrote it → application user determined by app
      registration → therefore per-customer app-reg is REQUIRED for per-customer BU placement. This is the
      structural reason, not an optimization.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="INCOMING §5 Item 1 (exact scope)">
      Remove: (1) the L272 branch on Model1Shared → HandleModel1Async, (2) `HandleModel1Async` method body
      (H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs:406-470), (3) `EntraAppRegOptions.SharedBffAppRegistrationId`, (4)
      `EntraAppRegOptions.SharedPlatformKeyVaultName`, (5) `EntraAppRegSharedVerifyRequest` record, (6)
      shared-path tests in `H3EntraAppRegHandlerTests.cs`. Result: H3 provisions ONE app-reg per customer,
      unconditionally, in both models.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="INCOMING §5 Item 1 IMPLICIT scope (grep-verified 2026-09-29)">
      §5 Item 1's explicit list is INCOMPLETE — the shared-path types have additional producers/consumers that
      must move atomically or compile breaks. FULL DELETION SET:
      (a) H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs: L272 branch + L274 call + `HandleModel1Async` (L406-470) + `BuildSharedKvUriReference`
          helper (L555-557 area) + `Model1Shared` local usage in `IsValidTenancyModel` (L546) — but see (i) below.
      (b) EntraAppRegOptions.cs: `SharedBffAppRegistrationId` (L64) + `SharedPlatformKeyVaultName` (L67) + class-header
          "NEW Model 1 fields (SharedBffAppRegistrationId/Audience/KeyVaultName)" note (L15).
      (c) IEntraAppRegProvisioner.cs: `VerifySharedAsync` interface method (L57-58) + `EntraAppRegSharedVerifyRequest`
          record (L134) + `EntraAppRegSharedVerifyOutcome` abstract record + 3 nested `Current`/`Drifted`/`Failure`
          records (L136-149) + all interface XML-doc mentions of "MODEL 1" verification.
      (d) GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs: `VerifySharedAsync` method (L262 through end of method) + all
          shared-app-reg helper methods it calls that are not shared with `ProvisionAsync`.
      (e) H3EntraAppRegHandlerTests.cs: every test citing `HandleModel1Async`, `VerifySharedAsync`,
          `SharedBffAppRegistrationId`, `SharedPlatformKeyVaultName`, `SharedAppRegConfigurationDrift`, or
          `MissingSharedAppRegConfig` — enumerate by grep at execution time.
      (f) EntraAppRegRejectionCodes.cs: `MissingSharedAppRegConfig` (L77-78) + `SharedAppRegConfigurationDrift`
          (L80-81) — mark with `[Obsolete("Retired 2026-09-29 per D-13 — H3 shared-app-reg branch deleted. Value
          kept for external-tool log/alerting historical stability per file-header STABILITY guidance.", error: false)]`
          rather than delete. The file-header STABILITY block explicitly permits this pattern: "add new codes as
          needed and mark old ones @[Obsolete] on removal". Historical operator UI filters + alerting rules keyed
          on these string constants (they've been in the codebase since task 130 Wave G-3) must not silently break.
      (g) FicVerificationState.NotApplicable (L217-218 in IEntraAppRegProvisioner.cs): XML-doc says "Model 1 — I6:
          zero per-customer app-reg/FIC objects". After Item 1, Model 1 ALSO creates a FIC. UPDATE the XML-doc to
          strike the Model 1 reference; KEEP the enum value as the defensive default (do NOT delete — enums are
          contracts; a fresh use case may reintroduce the semantic).
      (h) EntraAppRegOutputs.PendingKvWrites XML-doc (L182-187): "Empty for Model 1 (no writes — Model 1 only
          REFERENCES pre-existing shared-vault entries, nothing to commit)." — UPDATE to strike the Model 1 clause;
          both models now write.
      (i) DO NOT DELETE the `Model1Shared` const at H3:129 or the `IsValidTenancyModel` acceptance of it (L546).
          Post-Item-1, `Model1Shared` remains a VALID tenancy string — H3 accepts + routes it through the same
          per-customer creation path as Model2Dedicated. Item 2 will introduce the shared TenancyModel enum + kill
          the string literal comparisons everywhere in one atomic change. Removing `Model1Shared` acceptance here
          would fail every Model 1 run in the interim.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §6.5 (ADR Conflict Resolution Protocol)">
      Path C (pivot to comply) applies to Item 1: the code was written against the pre-D-13 world; D-13 is now
      binding; the code moves to comply. No Path A exception needed. If unexpected consumers surface (a new caller
      of the shared-app-reg helpers introduced by a parallel worktree since master merge), STOP and escalate per
      §6 rather than silently expanding scope.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §8 test-modifying override">
      Any task modifying `*Tests/**` requires UNCONDITIONAL FULL rigor + UNCONDITIONAL Step 9.5 quality gates
      (code-review + adr-check). This task modifies `H3EntraAppRegHandlerTests.cs` → both gates run.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A4 secret-free identity">
      Removing the shared-app-reg branch does NOT alter the ADR-028 A4 posture. The per-customer path already
      threads `RequireSecretFreeIdentity = true` through `EntraAppRegRequest` (constructor default, see
      IEntraAppRegProvisioner.cs L124-130) for both current Model 2 profiles. Model 1 post-Item-1 inherits that
      same secure default — no new `.WithClientSecret(...)` sites, no new secret-mint paths. Verify via ArchTest
      326/326 post-change (CredentialGuardTests + CredentialCensusTests). If a Model 1 profile is ever
      introduced that requires a non-secret-free identity, it must pass `false` EXPLICITLY at the H3 call site
      per the IEntraAppRegProvisioner.cs L118-123 "silent default of false is FORBIDDEN" rule.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 §7 KEEP-path forcing-function discipline">
      Deletions in `*Tests/**` may look like "weakening" the suite. They are NOT — the shared-path tests are
      testing a code path that no longer exists (D-13 retires it). Deleting them is the correct disposition.
      Do NOT scope-narrow or `[Skip]` them (that would leave lingering assertions on retired semantics). Delete
      them cleanly + note the deletion in commit message. New per-customer-unconditional tests should NOT be
      authored in this task — the existing `HandleModel2Async` test coverage plus the removed branch means the
      remaining tests already exercise the unified path. Only file follow-up test tasks if the deletion audit
      uncovers a genuine coverage gap (a shared-path test asserted something the unified path does NOT already
      assert).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="§4D Tenant Isolation invariants (design.md)">
      Removing the shared-app-reg branch strengthens I1/I5 (§4D):
      - I1 (no hardcoded default tenant): the shared-app-reg path always operated against `SpaarkeTenantId`
        regardless of the customer's `tenantId`; removing it removes a code path where per-customer tenant
        scoping was inert by construction.
      - I5 (per-tenant Graph tokens): the shared verification called `BuildTenantScopedGraphClient(_options.SpaarkeTenantId)`
        (see GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs:277) — a Spaarke-tenant-scoped Graph token used to read another
        tenant's app-reg configuration. Post-Item-1, every Graph call is per-customer-tenant-scoped by the
        Model 2 code path. No I5 change needed on our end; the invariant simply becomes universally applied.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>
      If grep for `SharedBffAppRegistrationId` OR `SharedPlatformKeyVaultName` OR `EntraAppRegSharedVerifyRequest`
      OR `EntraAppRegSharedVerifyOutcome` OR `VerifySharedAsync` OR `HandleModel1Async` OR `BuildSharedKvUriReference`
      returns a hit OUTSIDE these known sites: (H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs + EntraAppRegOptions.cs +
      IEntraAppRegProvisioner.cs + GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs + H3EntraAppRegHandlerTests.cs) —
      STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6. Likely causes: (a) parallel worktree added a new caller since
